onb, '"Model answer:\nHeadings (`h1`–`h6`) establish a hierarchy; paragraphs use `p`; lists use ordered (`ol`) or unordered (`ul`) containers with `li` items. Images are inserted with `img`; meaningful alternative text in `alt` helps users when the image cannot be seen and supports accessibility. Metadata such as character encoding belongs in `head`, while preformatted text can use `pre` when whitespace matters. Choose elements by meaning rather than visual appearance alone, keep heading levels logical, and provide useful text alternatives for informative images.\n\n8-mark marking guide: 2 marks for the core concept; 3 marks for accurate principles, steps or formulas; 2 marks for an example/application; 1 mark for a justified conclusion or check. A strong answer should explain the governing concept, justify the chosen method, check the result and acknowledge a relevant limitation."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

