VALUES (4400093531020121, ARRAY['"A page uses CSS animation on a decorative element and notices excessive movement for some users. What is the most appropriate improvement?"'::jsonb, '"A registration form lets users select multiple skills and one experience level. Which control design respects both requirements?"'::jsonb, '"A site loads HTML and images, but not CSS; the CSS URL returns 404. What should be done first?"'::jsonb, '"A developer makes a login page with HTTPS, but the server stores passwords as plain text. Which statement is correct?"'::jsonb, '"A site uses an IP address in a link instead of a domain. Which maintenance disadvantage is most plausible?"'::jsonb, '"A form submission loses the selected department. All radio inputs have different `name` attributes. What is the most likely markup-level issue?"'::jsonb, '"A layout must remain in the normal document flow and shift 8 px down from where it would normally appear. Which setting most directly fits?"'::jsonb, '"A page has a button that should submit a form, but clicking it resets the inputs. Which attribute value should be checked?"'::jsonb, '"A page needs a live feed where occasional dropped packets are acceptable and low latency matters more than guaranteed transport delivery. Which transport is a plausible choice?"'::jsonb, '"A website is moved from one IP address to another. The domain still resolves to the old address for some users. Which pair of actions is most relevant?"'::jsonb, '"A CSS background gradient is visible, but text contrast is poor on part of the card. What is the best fix?"'::jsonb, '"A site requires animations to run only when reduced motion is not requested. Which CSS organization best meets that constraint?"'::jsonb, '"A table header must label two columns, while a category heading spans two body rows. Which attributes serve those needs, respectively?"'::jsonb, '"An element must animate into view, but should not create a large movement for users who opt out of animation. What is the complete solution?"'::jsonb, '"A domain resolves correctly and the web server responds, but HTTPS warns that the certificate is for a different hostname. What should be investigated?"'::jsonb, '"An external stylesheet sets a heading teal, but a normal class rule changes it to purple and an ID rule changes it to navy. With equal origin/importance, which usually wins?"'::jsonb, '"A stylesheet change unexpectedly affects every paragraph on a site. Which selector is most likely responsible?"'::jsonb, '"An HTML page loads but the external CSS file returns 403 Forbidden. What should be checked before rewriting every selector?"'::jsonb, '"A site has duplicate IDs because the same `id=\"menu\"` is applied to every navigation item. What change is appropriate if they share the same styling?"'::jsonb, '"An element has `position: absolute; right: 0; bottom: 0;`. Which ancestor most directly determines its positioning reference when that ancestor is positioned?"'::jsonb, '"A class selector and an ID selector both set the same property on an element, with equal origin and no !important. Which usually wins?"'::jsonb, '"A developer must deliver a linked external CSS file and a semantic HTML page. Which verification set is most complete?"'::jsonb, '"A link works when the page is at `/index.html`, but not when the same code is moved to `/students/index.html`. It uses `href=\"syllabus.html\"`. Why?"'::jsonb, '"A tooltip is clipped inside a container that has overflow hidden. What should be inspected?"'::jsonb, '"A form needs one department choice and multiple interests; submitted values should be meaningful. Which combined setup is best?"'::jsonb, '"A browser can resolve a domain to an IP address, but the server returns an HTTP 404 for `/courses/sem1.html`. What is the most targeted interpretation?"'::jsonb, '"A developer places a tooltip beside a button using absolute positioning. It appears in the wrong place after layout changes. Which design change may make the placement more predictable?"'::jsonb, '"A card has width: 240px, padding: 12px on both sides and border: 3px on both sides under content-box sizing. Without margins, what is its outer width?"'::jsonb, '"A page must fit a card within a 300 px border-box width including 20 px padding on each side and 2 px borders. With `box-sizing: border-box`, what content width remains?"'::jsonb, '"External CSS is linked correctly, but inline style sets a different color on one element. Which explanation commonly applies?"'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Respect prefers-reduced-motion and provide a reduced-motion or no-animation state"'::jsonb, '"Increase movement until it becomes familiar"'::jsonb, '"Make animation mandatory in the HTML structure"'::jsonb, '"Use flashing text for emphasis"'::jsonb, '"One radio group for every skill and multiple levels"'::jsonb, '"Checkboxes for skills and a single named radio group for experience level"'::jsonb, '"A hidden input for every visible choice"'::jsonb, '"A submit button for each skill"'::jsonb, '"Rewrite every CSS rule without checking the URL"'::jsonb, '"Change the HTML title"'::jsonb, '"Correct the link/path or restore the stylesheet at the requested URL, then retest the page"'::jsonb, '"Replace all images with tables"'::jsonb, '"HTTPS automatically encrypts the database at rest"'::jsonb, '"Plain-text storage is safe because the form is hidden"'::jsonb, '"HTTPS protects data in transit; it does not by itself secure how the server stores passwords"'::jsonb, '"CSS can replace password storage controls"'::jsonb, '"A domain name cannot resolve to an IP"'::jsonb, '"The link must change if the service''s address changes, while a stable domain can be repointed via DNS"'::jsonb, '"HTTPS no longer works with domains"'::jsonb, '"An IP address is always encrypted"'::jsonb, '"The table has a thead"'::jsonb, '"The CSS background is a gradient"'::jsonb, '"The radio controls are not grouped under the same name, so their values are submitted as separate fields"'::jsonb