-- Basics of Web Designing | ESE | hard | TestId 4400093531020136 | theory
INSERT INTO public."TestsData" ("TestId", "Questions", "Options", "Answers")
VALUES (4400093531020136, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic problem involving html tables, headings and cell spanning, such as displaying a timetable with a heading spanning two columns. Present a reasoned approach, justify key decisions, and state an important limitation or verification check."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic problem involving html forms and controls, such as collecting a student''s name, choice and confirmation. Present a reasoned approach, justify key decisions, and state an important limitation or verification check."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic problem involving css rules, selectors and property declarations, such as applying one style to every paragraph and a separate style to one class. Present a reasoned approach, justify key decisions, and state an important limitation or verification check."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic problem involving stylesheet types and advanced css effects, such as maintaining a consistent theme and adding a transition to a card. Present a reasoned approach, justify key decisions, and state an important limitation or verification check."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer:\nAn HTML table uses `table` as its container, `tr` for rows, and `th` or `td` for header and data cells. `thead`, `tbody` and `tfoot` group relevant parts of the table. `colspan` makes a cell span multiple columns; `rowspan` makes it span multiple rows. These attributes change the table grid, so the number and arrangement of cells must remain consistent. Tables should represent tabular data rather than general page layout, and header cells should clearly identify the meaning of each column or row.\n\n8-mark marking guide: 2 marks for the core concept; 3 marks for accurate principles, steps or formulas; 2 marks for an example/application; 1 mark for a justified conclusion or check. A strong answer should explain the governing concept, justify the chosen method, check the result and acknowledge a relevant limitation."'::jsonb, '"Model answer:\nA `form` groups controls and defines how submitted data is sent. `input` supports different controls such as text, radio, checkbox, hidden and submit/reset inputs; `select` provides a drop-down list. Each relevant control needs a meaningful name, and labels should identify controls clearly. Radio buttons are suited to one choice from a group; checkboxes allow independent selections. Client-side validation improves usability but should not replace server-side validation. Sensitive information should be transmitted over HTTPS and processed securely.\n\n8-mark marking guide: 2 marks for the core concept; 3 marks for accurate principles, steps or formulas; 2 marks for an example/application; 1 mark for a justified conclusion or check. A strong answer should explain the governing concept, justify the chosen method, check the result and acknowledge a relevant limitation."'::jsonb, '"Model answer:\nA CSS rule has a selector and a declaration block. Each declaration contains a property and value, for example `color: navy;`. Type selectors target elements, class selectors begin with a dot, and ID selectors begin with a hash. Selectors determine which elements match; the cascade, specificity and source order help decide which declaration applies when rules conflict. Keep declarations syntactically valid, use reusable classes for repeated styling, and avoid relying on unnecessarily specific selectors that make future changes difficult.\n\n8-mark marking guide: 2 marks for the core concept; 3 marks for accurate principles, steps or formulas; 2 marks for an example/application; 1 mark for a justified conclusion or check. A strong answer should explain the governing concept, justify the chosen method, check the result and acknowledge a relevant limitation."'::jsonb, '"Model answer:\nInline CSS is written on an element, embedded CSS inside a `style` element, and external CSS in a separate linked file; external styles are usually easiest to reuse and maintain across pages. CSS controls colors, fonts, text effects, backgrounds and positioning. Gradients create transitions between colors, shadows add depth, transforms change an element''s visual geometry, and animations or transitions change presentation over time. Tooltips need accessible interaction and positioning. Effects should improve clarity, preserve readability and remain usable across screen sizes.\n\n8-mark marking guide: 2 marks for the core concept; 3 marks for accurate principles, steps or formulas; 2 marks for an example/application; 1 mark for a justified conclusion or check. A strong answer should explain the governing concept, justify the chosen method, check the result and acknowledge a relevant limitation."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

-- Bharatiya Knowledge System | Mid 1 | easy | TestId 440099110101011 | theory
INSERT INTO public."TestsData" ("TestId", "Questions", "Options", "Answers")
VALUES (440099110101011, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Explain Meaning, scope and classification of Bharatiya Knowledge Systems. Describe its meaning or purpose, principal features or steps, and one relevant example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Caturdasa-Vidyasthana and the traditional knowledge disciplines. Describe its meaning or purpose, principal features or steps, and one relevant example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain The four Vedas and their broad roles. Describe its meaning or purpose, principal features or steps, and one relevant example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Vedangas and their role in studying Vedic texts. Describe its meaning or purpose, principal features or steps, and one relevant example."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer:\nBharatiya Knowledge Systems (BKS) refers to knowledge traditions developed and transmitted in the Indian subcontinent across intellectual, practical, cultural and philosophical fields. Depending on the syllabus framework, areas include Vedic and philosophical literature, language sciences, mathematics, astronomy, medicine, arts, engineering, architecture and environmental practices. Classification helps organize sources and disciplines without treating every tradition as identical. A sound explanation names the field, identifies its historical or textual context, and distinguishes documented practices from later interpretation. Claims should be supported by the relevant text, artifact or historical evidence rather than generalized to all people or periods.\n\n8-mark marking guide: 2 marks for the core concept; 3 marks for accurate principles, steps or formulas; 2 marks for an example/application; 1 mark for a justified conclusion or check. A strong answer should define the concept and organize the main points clearly."'::jsonb, '"Model answer:\nCaturdasa-Vidyasthana is a traditional classification of fourteen knowledge disciplines. A common presentation counts the four Vedas, six Vedangas and four additional knowledge traditions such as Mimamsa, Nyaya, Purana and Dharmashastra, though descriptions can vary by source. The framework shows how textual study, interpretation, language, ritual, reasoning and normative traditions were organized. When explaining it, identify the components, show how the categories relate, and note that the scheme is a traditional taxonomy rather than a modern university department list.\n\n8-mark marking guide: 2 marks for the core concept; 3 marks for accurate principles, steps or formulas; 2 marks for an example/application; 1 mark for a justified conclusion or check. A strong answer should define the concept and organize the main points clearly."'::jsonb, '"Model answer:\nThe four Vedas are Rigveda, Samaveda, Yajurveda and Atharvaveda. The Rigveda is known for hymns; the Samaveda is closely associated with chants and melodies; the Yajurveda contains prose formulas and material related to ritual performance; and the Atharvaveda includes hymns and material concerning everyday life and ritual. Their contents overlap and their textual traditions are complex, so descriptions should be broad rather than absolute. Explain each name and its principal association, and avoid attributing every later scientific or social idea directly to all four Vedas.\n\n8-mark marking guide: 2 marks for the core concept; 3 marks for accurate principles, steps or formulas; 2 marks for an example/application; 1 mark for a justified conclusion or check. A strong answer should define the concept and organize the main points clearly."'::jsonb, '"Model answer:\nThe six Vedangas are Shiksha (phonetics/pronunciation), Chandas (metre), Vyakarana (grammar), Nirukta (etymology or explanation of words), Kalpa (ritual procedure) and Jyotisha (astronomical/calendrical timing). They support accurate recitation, interpretation and performance connected with Vedic literature. They are complementary: phonetics helps pronunciation, grammar analyzes forms, metre studies poetic structure, and Jyotisha relates to timekeeping. A complete answer names the six fields and explains at least one practical role of each instead of confusing them with modern engineering subjects.\n\n8-mark marking guide: 2 marks for the core concept; 3 marks for accurate principles, steps or formulas; 2 marks for an example/application; 1 mark for a justified conclusion or check. A strong answer should define the concept and organize the main points clearly."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

-- Bharatiya Knowledge System | Mid 1 | easy | TestId 440099110101012 | theory
INSERT INTO public."TestsData" ("TestId", "Questions", "Options", "Answers")
VALUES (440099110101012, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Explain Meaning, scope and classification of Bharatiya Knowledge Systems. Describe its meaning or purpose, principal features or steps, and one relevant example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Caturdasa-Vidyasthana and the traditional knowledge disciplines. Describe its meaning or purpose, principal features or steps, and one relevant example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Purana and Itihasa as sources of knowledge and wisdom. Describe its meaning or purpose, principal features or steps, and one relevant example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Indian number traditions, measurement, mathematics and Jyotisha. Describe its meaning or purpose, principal features or steps, and one relevant example."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer:\nBharatiya Knowledge Systems (BKS) refers to knowledge traditions developed and transmitted in the Indian subcontinent across intellectual, practical, cultural and philosophical fields. Depending on the syllabus framework, areas include Vedic and philosophical literature, language sciences, mathematics, astronomy, medicine, arts, engineering, architecture and environmental practices. Classification helps organize sources and disciplines without treating every tradition as identical. A sound explanation names the field, identifies its historical or textual context, and distinguishes documented practices from later interpretation. Claims should be supported by the relevant text, artifact or historical evidence rather than generalized to all people or periods.\n\n8-mark marking guide: 2 marks for the core concept; 3 marks for accurate principles, steps or formulas; 2 marks for an example/application; 1 mark for a justified conclusion or check. A strong answer should define the concept and organize the main points clearly."'::jsonb, '"Model answer:\nCaturdasa-Vidyasthana is a traditional classification of fourteen knowledge disciplines. A common presentation counts the four Vedas, six Vedangas and four additional knowledge traditions such as Mimamsa, Nyaya, Purana and Dharmashastra, though descriptions can vary by source. The framework shows how textual study, interpretation, language, ritual, reasoning and normative traditions were organized. When explaining it, identify the components, show how the categories relate, and note that the scheme is a traditional taxonomy rather than a modern university department list.\n\n8-mark marking guide: 2 marks for the core concept; 3 marks for accurate principles, steps or formulas; 2 marks for an example/application; 1 mark for a justified conclusion or check. A strong answer should define the concept and organize the main points clearly."'::jsonb, '"Model answer:\nPurana literature commonly combines cosmology, genealogies, narratives, teachings and accounts of sacred places or practices. Itihasa traditionally refers especially to the Ramayana and Mahabharata and is often studied as narrative literature carrying ethical, political and philosophical reflection. Their purposes and structures differ, but both have been transmitted through layered textual and interpretive traditions. A careful academic discussion identifies the work and passage, distinguishes narrative or normative meaning from independently verified historical fact, and explains how the text has influenced cultural memory, values and interpretation.\n\n8-mark marking guide: 2 marks for the core concept; 3 marks for accurate principles, steps or formulas; 2 marks for an example/application; 1 mark for a justified conclusion or check. A strong answer should define the concept and organize the main points clearly."'::jsonb, '"Model answer:\nThe syllabus connects historical number systems and units for time, distance and weight with arithmetic, geometry, trigonometry, algebra and astronomy. Vedanga Jyotisha concerns calendrical and astronomical timing in a traditional textual setting. A strong explanation distinguishes numerical notation from units of measurement, names the mathematical operation or unit being discussed, and explains how measurement enables comparison and calculation. Claims about origins or historical priority should be tied to specific evidence. For a calendar example, describe how a chosen timekeeping rule organizes recurring cycles rather than claiming that every historical calendar used an identical method.\n\n8-mark marking guide: 2 marks for the core concept; 3 marks for accurate principles, steps or formulas; 2 marks for an example/application; 1 mark for a justified conclusion or check. A strong answer should define the concept and organize the main points clearly."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

