"'::jsonb, '"An ethical-living presentation needs to include duty, prosperity, enjoyment and liberation. What structure avoids omitting any Purushartha?"'::jsonb, '"A student classifies six study notes: pronunciation, ritual method, grammar, word etymology, metre and calendar calculation. Which mapping places every note correctly?"'::jsonb, '"A comparison of two traditional water systems finds one suited to seasonal rainfall and another to a different local environment. Which conclusion is strongest?"'::jsonb, '"A presentation links traditional measurement with modern scientific units. Which method is strongest?"'::jsonb, '"A student wants to distinguish a supported syllabus fact from a historical hypothesis. Which practice is best?"'::jsonb, '"A case says a person prioritizes ethical duty, livelihood, enjoyment and liberation. Which framework is being applied?"'::jsonb, '"A calendar dataset contains dates for ritual observances, but no source explains its calculation rules. What is the most defensible research step?"'::jsonb, '"Which research claim most clearly stays within the outline when discussing ancient Indian mathematics?"'::jsonb, '"A lesson compares Puranas, Itihasa and the Vedic corpus. Which categorization is most consistent with the syllabus?"'::jsonb, '"A student must compare an epic narrative with a modern engineering record. Which approach matches the course framing of Itihasa as a source of wisdom?"'::jsonb, '"A researcher wants to claim a specific metal technology was used at a named site, but the course outline only lists metalworking generally. What should they do?"'::jsonb, '"A project combines evidence about a historic water system with a modern proposal. Which conclusion is best supported by the syllabus without overclaiming?"'::jsonb, '"A student has 14 study headings and must sort them into the conventional Caturdaśa-Vidyāsthāna scheme. Which composition should guide the first pass?"'::jsonb, '"A report combines ancient mathematics and astronomy but has only evidence about one calendar. How should the claim be narrowed?"'::jsonb, '"Which plan best evaluates a claim that ancient textile dyeing was a technical speciality?"'::jsonb, '"A report compares an irrigation canal, a rainwater harvesting structure and a town plan. Which source-area grouping best supports the comparison?"'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"NLP, HTML forms and email signatures"'::jsonb, '"Vastu Shastra, civil architecture and temple architecture"'::jsonb, '"HCF, LCM and polynomial identities"'::jsonb, '"Recycle Bin and shell commands"'::jsonb, '"It extrapolates from one example to a universal historical claim without sufficient evidence"'::jsonb, '"It distinguishes source and interpretation"'::jsonb, '"It cites the number system"'::jsonb, '"It defines geometry too precisely"'::jsonb, '"It aligns with the syllabus topic, but a specific computational performance claim still needs evidence"'::jsonb, '"It proves every NLP system requires Sanskrit"'::jsonb, '"It establishes a metalworking technique"'::jsonb, '"It is unrelated because computation never uses language structure"'::jsonb, '"Caturdaśa refers only to four Vedas"'::jsonb, '"Caturdaśa-Vidyāsthāna is a 14-part knowledge classification; the four Ashramas are life stages"'::jsonb, '"Both mean the four goals of life"'::jsonb, '"Ashramas are six Vedangas"'::jsonb, '"Both are units of distance"'::jsonb, '"Moksha refers to liberation; Artha is the Purushartha associated with material means"'::jsonb, '"Moksha is grammar and Artha is metre"'::jsonb, '"Both are Vedas"'::jsonb, '"Irrigation/water management and transportation/trading techniques"'::jsonb, '"Inline and external CSS"'::jsonb, '"Shiksha and Chandas"'::jsonb, '"Brahmacharya and Sannyasa"'::jsonb, '"Discuss only the mechanical keyboard"'::jsonb, '"Explain the stated relationship between Sanskrit and natural language processing"'::jsonb, '"Claim that all software must be written in Sanskrit"'::jsonb, '"Replace language analysis with a calendar chart"'::jsonb, '"Treat them as one identical process"'::jsonb, '"Classify every theme as an Ashrama"'::jsonb, '"Organize them as separate technology themes and compare each practice using relevant evidence and constraints"'::jsonb, '"Put all evidence under the four Vedas"'::jsonb, '"Use only the modern name of the reservoir"'::jsonb, '"Infer details solely from the general syllabus"'::jsonb, '"Assume every reservoir belongs to the same tradition"'::jsonb, '"Combine site-specific records or credible studies with analysis of storage, supply and setting"'::jsonb, '"Moksha is a measurement of weight"'::jsonb, '"They are all names for poetic metre"'::jsonb, '"Karma and rebirth concern action and continuing existence; Moksha concerns liberation"'::jsonb, '"Karma is a computer peripheral"'::jsonb, '"This site provides an example of textile dyeing practice; broader prevalence needs additional evidence"'::jsonb, '"The site proves a universal rule"'::jsonb, '"All places used precisely the same technique"'::jsonb, '"Textile dyeing is a Purushartha"'::jsonb, '"Both are types of temple architecture"'::jsonb, '"Yajurveda is metre; Samaveda is grammar"'::jsonb, '"Yajurveda is associated with ritual formulas; Samaveda with chants/melodies"'::jsonb, '"Yajurveda is a Purana; Samaveda is a Vedanga"'::jsonb, '"The photo proves the site''s exact date"'::jsonb, '"A photograph alone gives all design rules"'::jsonb, '"Urban planning is not a syllabus topic"'::jsonb, '"The evidence is insufficient to support a detailed historical interpretation"'::jsonb, '"A list of the four Vedas only"'::jsonb, '"An unrelated HTML layout"'::jsonb, '"A statement that all grids are Vastu-based"'::jsonb, '"Source-specific historical documentation linking the plan to the relevant planning principles"'::jsonb, '"Rigveda, Samaveda, Chandas and Kalpa"'::jsonb, '"Time, distance, weight and calendars"'::jsonb, '"Dharma, Artha, Kama and Moksha"'::jsonb, '"Brahmacharya, Grihastha, Nyaya and Vastu"'::jsonb, '"