erbs express actions or states; adjectives modify nouns; adverbs modify verbs, adjectives or other adverbs. Prepositions express relationships, conjunctions connect units, and interjections express reactions. A word''s part of speech depends on how it functions in the sentence, not only on its spelling. During editing, identify the word''s role and check whether modifiers are placed clearly and whether each clause is complete.\n\n8-mark marking guide: 2 marks for the core concept; 3 marks for accurate principles, steps or formulas; 2 marks for an example/application; 1 mark for a justified conclusion or check. A strong answer should connect the concept to the stated example, explain the steps in order and justify the outcome."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

