VALUES (4409191201030121, ARRAY['"A formal email asks a faculty member to review a project proposal and needs to mention an attached file. Which subject and opening are strongest?"'::jsonb, '"Which sentence preserves parallel construction in a project objective list?"'::jsonb, '"A text indicates that a college is considering a new timetable but has not approved it. Which statement is justified?"'::jsonb, '"A presenter has evidence that a pilot worked with 12 participants. Which conclusion is best calibrated to the evidence?"'::jsonb, '"An application requests leave from 8 to 10 January. Which detail is essential to make the request actionable?"'::jsonb, '"A passage describes a trial at one campus and says the approach ''may be useful elsewhere''. Which interpretation respects the wording?"'::jsonb, '"A recommendation is supported by three measurements, but one was collected under different conditions. How should it be presented?"'::jsonb, '"An email contains a vague subject, an attachment with an unclear filename, and a deadline only in the final paragraph. Which revision most improves usability?"'::jsonb, '"An email requests an urgent document, but the recipient''s role is unclear and the deadline is unrealistic. What is the best communication strategy?"'::jsonb, '"Choose the best revision: “After reviewing the data, the conclusion was changed by the analyst because it was incomplete.”"'::jsonb, '"A formal application contains long background paragraphs but never states the requested action. What is the critical repair?"'::jsonb, '"A speaker is challenged about a statistic but is unsure of the source. What is the most credible response?"'::jsonb, '"A technician''s instructions must describe four actions in the order performed. Which wording has the strongest procedural clarity?"'::jsonb, '"Choose the only grammatically correct sentence."'::jsonb, '"Choose the sentence that correctly combines a past event completed before another past event."'::jsonb, '"During Q&A, 