VALUES (4409191201030133, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic problem involving planning and writing a clear formal email, such as requesting a meeting with a faculty member about a lab submission. Present a reasoned approach, justify key decisions, and state an important limitation or verification check."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic problem involving structure and tone of a formal application, such as applying for permission to attend an academic event. Present a reasoned approach, justify key decisions, and state an important limitation or verification check."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic problem involving writing an event or industrial-visit report, such as reporting a college visit with observations and outcomes. Present a reasoned approach, justify key decisions, and state an important limitation or verification check."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic problem involving planning and organizing an assignment, such as turning a broad topic into a well-structured short assignment. Present a reasoned approach, justify key decisions, and state an important limitation or verification check."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer:\nA formal email needs a specific subject line, an appropriate greeting, a concise opening that states the purpose, organized details, a clear request or next step, a courteous closing and the sender''s name. Use a professional tone, correct grammar and paragraphs that each serve one purpose. Check the recipient address and any attachment before sending. Add CC only for people who need visibility and BCC when recipients should not see one another''s addresses. Do not place confidential information in unnecessary recipients or subject lines.\n\n8-mark marking guide: 2 marks for the core concept; 3 marks for accurate principles, steps or formulas; 2 marks for an example/application; 1 mark for a justified conclusion or check. A strong answer should explain the governing concept, justify the chosen method, check the result and acknowledge a relevant limitation."'::jsonb, '"Model answer:\nA formal application identifies the recipient, date, subject and applicant, then states the request clearly and gives only relevant reasons or supporting details. It uses a respectful salutation, concise body paragraphs, a clear closing and the required signature or identification. The writer should maintain a formal tone, avoid slang and emotional exaggeration, and ensure the requested action is explicit. Proofread names, dates and attachments. A good application lets the recipient understand what is being requested, why it is justified and what response or approval is needed.\n\n8-mark marking guide: 2 marks for the core concept; 3 marks for accurate principles, steps or formulas; 2 marks for an example/application; 1 mark for a justified conclusion or check. A strong answer should explain the governing concept, justify the chosen method, check the result and acknowledge a relevant limitation."'::jsonb, '"Model answer:\nA report records an event objectively and in a structured order. Include a meaningful title, date and place, purpose, participants, major activities, observations, outcomes and a conclusion or recommendations where appropriate. Arrange events chronologically or under clear headings and use past tense for completed activities. Separate observed facts from personal opinion and support claims with reliable details. Proofread names and dates, keep the language concise, and make the report useful to a reader who did not attend the event.\n\n8-mark marking guide: 2 marks for the core concept; 3 marks for accurate principles, steps or formulas; 2 marks for an example/application; 1 mark for a justified conclusion or check. A strong answer should explain the governing concept, justify the chosen method, check the result and acknowledge a relevant limitation."'::jsonb, '"Model answer:\nBegin by interpreting the task and identifying the expected scope. Gather relevant sources, make an outline, and organize the introduction, main discussion and conclusion in a logical sequence. Each paragraph should develop one idea and connect it to the overall argument. Use accurate examples and acknowledge sources in the required format; do not copy text without attribution. Revise for completeness, flow, factual accuracy and grammar, then check formatting and submission requirements. A strong assignment answers the exact question rather than merely collecting loosely related information.\n\n8-mark marking guide: 2 marks for the core concept; 3 marks for accurate principles, steps or formulas; 2 marks for an example/application; 1 mark for a justified conclusion or check. A strong answer should explain the governing concept, justify the chosen method, check the result and acknowledge a relevant limitation."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

-- Communication Skills-I | ESE | hard | TestId 4409191201030134 | theory
INSERT INTO public."TestsData" ("TestId", "Questions", "Options", "Answers")
VALUES (4409191201030134, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic problem involving planning and writing a clear formal email, such as requesting a meeting with a faculty member about a lab submission. Present a reasoned approach, justify key decisions, and state an important limitation or verification check."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic problem involving structure and tone of a formal application, such as applying for permission to attend an academic event. Present a reasoned approach, justify key decisions, and state an important limitation or verification check."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic problem involving coherence, paragraphing and proofreading, such as editing a draft whose sentences are individually correct but poorly connected. Present a reasoned approach, justify key decisions, and state an important limitation or verification check."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic problem involving combining reading and writing skills for a source-based response, such as summarizing an article without adding claims the author did not make. Present a reasoned approach, justify key decisions, and state an important limitation or verification check."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer:\nA formal email needs a specific subject line, an appropriate greeting, a concise opening that states the purpose, organized details, a clear request or next step, a courteous closing and the sender''s name. Use a professional tone, correct grammar and paragraphs that each serve one purpose. Check the recipient address and any attachment before sending. Add CC only for people who need visibility and BCC when recipients should not see one another''s addresses. Do not place confidential information in unnecessary recipients or subject lines.\n\n8-mark marking guide: 2 marks for the core concept; 3 marks for accurate principles, steps or formulas; 2 marks for an example/application; 1 mark for a justified conclusion or check. A strong answer should explain the governing concept, justify the chosen method, check the result and acknowledge a relevant limitation."'::jsonb, '"Model answer:\nA formal application identifies the recipient, date, subject and applicant, then states the request clearly and gives only relevant reasons or supporting details. It uses a respectful salutation, concise body paragraphs, a clear closing and the required signature or identification. The writer should maintain a formal tone, avoid slang and emotional exaggeration, and ensure the requested action is explicit. Proofread names, dates and attachments. A good application lets the recipient understand what is being requested, why it is justified and what response or approval is needed.\n\n8-mark marking guide: 2 marks for the core concept; 3 marks for accurate principles, steps or formulas; 2 marks for an example/application; 1 mark for a justified conclusion or check. A strong answer should explain the governing concept, justify the chosen method, check the result and acknowledge a relevant limitation."'::jsonb, '"Model answer:\nA coherent text has a clear purpose, logical order and links between ideas. A paragraph usually has one main point supported by explanation or evidence; transitions show addition, contrast, cause or sequence. Pronouns and repeated key terms should make references clear. Proofreading should check sentence completeness, tense consistency, subject–verb agreement, punctuation, spelling and word choice. Revision focuses first on meaning and structure, then on sentence-level correctness. Read the draft from the reader''s perspective and remove material that does not support the purpose.\n\n8-mark marking guide: 2 marks for the core concept; 3 marks for accurate principles, steps or formulas; 2 marks for an example/application; 1 mark for a justified conclusion or check. A strong answer should explain the governing concept, justify the chosen method, check the result and acknowledge a relevant limitation."'::jsonb, '"Model answer:\nRead the source to identify its central claim, supporting evidence, structure and purpose. Distinguish facts, opinions and inferences, then make brief notes using keywords. Draft a response in your own words, preserving the source''s meaning and giving credit where required. Do not add unsupported conclusions or copy sentences simply by replacing a few words. Review whether the response answers the prompt, reflects the source fairly and follows the requested length and format. Reading accuracy is the foundation for clear source-based writing.\n\n8-mark marking guide: 2 marks for the core concept; 3 marks for accurate principles, steps or formulas; 2 marks for an example/application; 1 mark for a justified conclusion or check. A strong answer should explain the governing concept, justify the chosen method, check the result and acknowledge a relevant limitation."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

