ld explain the governing concept, justify the chosen method, check the result and acknowledge a relevant limitation."'::jsonb, '"Model answer:\nAn isometric drawing shows three principal axes equally inclined in the representation, commonly 120 degrees apart. Isometric projection uses foreshortened lengths along the axes and therefore an isometric scale; an isometric view/drawing often uses true lengths along isometric axes as prescribed in the course. To construct an object, establish the axes, transfer width, depth and height from the orthographic views, add faces and circular features with suitable isometric constructions, then remove unnecessary construction lines. Check that all dimensions correspond to the original orthographic views.\n\n8-mark marking guide: 2 marks for the core concept; 3 marks for accurate principles, steps or formulas; 2 marks for an example/application; 1 mark for a justified conclusion or check. A strong answer should explain the governing concept, justify the chosen method, check the result and acknowledge a relevant limitation."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

