-- Indian Constitution | Mid 1 | easy | TestId 440091210101011 | mcq
INSERT INTO public."TestsData" ("TestId", "Questions", "Options", "Answers")
VALUES (440091210101011, ARRAY['"A person argues that the Constitution exists only to empower the government. Which Preamble value most clearly contradicts an unlimited-power view?"'::jsonb, '"A citizen''s speech is restricted by a law. Which is the most accurate way to evaluate the restriction under Article 19?"'::jsonb, '"A citizen challenges an order affecting personal liberty. The authority claims Article 21 only applies when a law is completely absent, not when procedure exists but is arbitrary. Which response best reflects modern constitutional reasoning at course level?"'::jsonb, '"The Preamble''s words ''Secular'' and ''Socialist'' were inserted by an amendment. Which statement about that history is correct?"'::jsonb, '"A public authority refuses the same legal protection to two people in materially identical circumstances without a relevant reason. Which constitutional principle is most directly raised?"'::jsonb, '"Which statement best describes the ECI''s constitutional role?"'::jsonb, '"A constitutional issue concerns equal treatment, personal liberty and a policy directive. Which response is methodologically sound?"'::jsonb, '"A citizen damages public property during a protest. Which Fundamental Duty is most directly relevant to the conduct?"'::jsonb, '"Which body framed and adopted the Constitution before it came into force?"'::jsonb, '"Which amendment added the words Socialist, Secular and Integrity to the Preamble?"'::jsonb, '"Which Article guarantees equality before the law and equal protection of the laws?"'::jsonb, '"What is the general legal status of Fundamental Duties?"'::jsonb, '"Which set contains the four ideals expressly stated in the Preamble?"'::jsonb, '"A local government officer claims their administrative decisions are outside constitutional limits because the office is local, not national. Which principle best answers that claim?"'::jsonb, '"A claimant argues that because a policy appears in Part IV, courts must enforce it as if it were a Fundamental Right. Which constitutional text most directly challenges that claim?"'::jsonb, '"Fundamental Duties are mainly listed in:"'::jsonb, '"Who is the constitutional head of a state in India?"'::jsonb, '"On which date did the Constitution of India come into effect?"'::jsonb, '"A law restricts a citizen''s speech to address a public concern. The citizen argues Article 19 makes all restrictions invalid. Which reasoning is most defensible?"'::jsonb, '"An official says Article 14 guarantees identical treatment even where relevant circumstances differ. Which statement is more accurate?"'::jsonb, '"A state policy seeks environmental improvement, but an official arbitrarily denies access to a public benefit. What is a balanced analysis?"'::jsonb, '"Which concept means that public power is exercised under and limited by the Constitution?"'::jsonb, '"A Fundamental Duty to protect the environment is cited to automatically deny a person''s otherwise lawful speech. Which conclusion is most careful?"'::jsonb, '"A person argues that a Fundamental Right can never be limited. Which response best fits the course topics?"'::jsonb, '"A policy objective appears in Part IV, but a petitioner wants a court order solely to enforce it as a Directive Principle. Which constitutional statement is most relevant?"'::jsonb, '"Which Article lists Fundamental Duties?"'::jsonb, '"Directive Principles of State Policy are found in:"'::jsonb, '"Which amendment constitutionalized the Panchayati Raj framework?"'::jsonb, '"A law classifies citizens by a criterion unrelated to its stated goal; affected people also claim the criterion burdens an Article 19 freedom. What is the strongest analytical approach?"'::jsonb, '"When did the Constitution of India come into force?"'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Justice, liberty, equality and fraternity as constitutional objectives"'::jsonb, '"Abolition of judicial review"'::jsonb, '"Absolute executive discretion"'::jsonb, '"Unlimited terms for every elected body"'::jsonb, '"Check the relevant freedom and whether the restriction fits a constitutionally permitted ground and is reasonable"'::jsonb, '"Any restriction is automatically unconstitutional"'::jsonb, '"Article 19 permits no restrictions in any circumstances"'::jsonb, '"Treat Article 19 as a duty rather than a right"'::jsonb, '"Any written procedure automatically validates every deprivation"'::jsonb, '"Article 14 and 21 cannot ever be considered together"'::jsonb, '"Article 21 only applies during elections"'::jsonb, '"Article 21 protection includes scrutiny of the legal procedure affecting life and liberty; the existence of a procedure alone does not end analysis"'::jsonb, '"They were included only by the 86th Amendment"'::jsonb, '"They were added to the original text in 1947"'::jsonb, '"They were added by the 42nd Amendment in 1976"'::jsonb, '"They are found only in Article 324"'::jsonb, '"Election administration under Article 324"'::jsonb, '"Freedom of speech under Article 19 only"'::jsonb, '"Equality before law and equal protection under Article 14"'::jsonb, '"Fundamental Duty under Article 51A only"'::jsonb, '"It supervises specified electoral rolls and elections under Article 324"'::jsonb, '"It appoints all Governors"'::jsonb, '"It administers all municipal services"'::jsonb, '"It makes all criminal laws"'::jsonb, '"Apply only Article 51A to every dispute"'::jsonb, '"Assume Part IV repeals Part III"'::jsonb, '"Refer it to a municipal corporation as the final constitutional court"'::jsonb, '"Identify the separate questions under Article 14, Article 21 and Part IV, then interpret them together rather than treating one as automatic trump"'::jsonb, '"Duty to vote in every election as stated in Article 51A"'::jsonb, '"Duty to safeguard public property and abjure violence"'::jsonb, '"Duty to serve as a judge"'::jsonb, '"Duty to protect the environment only"'::jsonb, '"Union Cabinet"'::jsonb, '"Constituent Assembly"'::jsonb, '"Supreme Court"'::jsonb, '"Election Commission"'::jsonb, '"42nd Amendment"'::jsonb, '"24th Amendment"'::jsonb, '"86th Amendment"'::jsonb, '"44th Amendment"'::jsonb, '"Article 19"'::jsonb, '"Article 21"'::jsonb, '"Article 14"'::jsonb, '"Article 32 only"'::jsonb, '"They are constitutional duties in Part IVA, generally not directly enforceable like Fundamental Rights"'::jsonb, '"They are private recommendations outside the Constitution"'::jsonb, '"They apply only to local bodies"'::jsonb, '"They replace all Fundamental Rights"'::jsonb, '"Security, growth, wealth and unity"'::jsonb, '"Liberty, authority, property and order"'::jsonb, '"Justice, liberty, equality and fraternity"'::jsonb, '"Power, duty, faith and discipline"'::jsonb, '"Constitutionalism applies only during general elections"'::jsonb, '"Only Parliament must follow law"'::jsonb, '"Public authorities at all levels must act within applicable constitutional and legal limits"'::jsonb, '"Fundamental Rights apply only to Union ministers"'::jsonb, '"Article 51A(k)"'::jsonb, '"Article 37"'::jsonb, '"Article 21"'::jsonb, '"Article 324"'::jsonb, '"Part III"'::jsonb, '"Part IX only"'::jsonb, '"Part IVA"'::jsonb, '"Part I"'::jsonb, '"Chief Minister"'::jsonb, '"Governor"'::jsonb, '"Speaker of the Assembly"'::jsonb, '"District Collector"'::jsonb, '"26 January 1950"'::jsonb, '"1 January 1951"'::jsonb, '"26 November 1949"'::jsonb, '"15 August 1947"'::jsonb, '"Treat the restriction as a Fundamental Duty"'::jsonb, '"Declare every speech restriction invalid without examining the provision"'::jsonb, '"Decide solely by the location of the person''s district"'::jsonb, '"Identify the relevant Article 19 freedom and test whether the restriction is reasonable and falls within a constitutionally permitted ground"'::jsonb, '"Article 14 abolishes all classification"'::jsonb, '"Equality requires equal protection and bars arbitrary discrimination, but reasonable classification may be constitutionally permitted"'::jsonb, '"Article 14 only concerns local elections"'::jsonb, '"Article 14 applies only to elected officials"'::jsonb, '"Assume Fundamental Duties erase all legal procedures"'::jsonb, '"Treat the environmental aim as an automatic exemption from equality"'::jsonb, '"Recognize the environmental aim and Article 51A duty, while also assessing whether the decision complies with applicable rights such as Article 14"'::jsonb, '"Assume Article 14 applies only during elections"'::jsonb, '"Administrative convenience"'::jsonb, '"Constitutionalism"'::jsonb, '"Absolute executive discretion"'::jsonb, '"Rule by personal preference"'::jsonb, '"Environmental protection is not mentioned in Article 51A"'::jsonb, '"The duty is relevant, but a restriction on speech must still be assessed under the constitutional provisions governing that freedom"'::jsonb, '"Fundamental Duties automatically override every right"'::jsonb, '"Article 51A applies only to municipal officers"'::jsonb, '"Some rights, including Article 19 freedoms, are subject to constitutionally specified restrictions"'::jsonb, '"Part III contains only non-binding policy aims"'::jsonb, '"Article 21 applies only to elected legislators"'::jsonb, '"All Fundamental Rights can be cancelled by an ordinary officer"'::jsonb, '"Part IV is the same as Part III"'::jsonb, '"All policies in Part IV are criminal provisions"'::jsonb, '"Part IV applies only during elections"'::jsonb, '"Article 37 states Directive Principles are not enforceable by courts, while remaining fundamental in governance"'::jsonb, '"Article 32"'::jsonb, '"Article 19"'::jsonb, '"Article 14"'::jsonb, '"Article 51A"'::jsonb, '"Part IVA"'::jsonb, '"Part III"'::jsonb, '"Part V only"'::jsonb, '"Part IV"'::jsonb, '"73rd Amendment"'::jsonb, '"44th Amendment"'::jsonb, '"86th Amendment"'::jsonb, '"42nd Amendment"'::jsonb, '"Assume a single Article automatically decides all claims"'::jsonb, '"Refer the policy to a Zila Panchayat for constitutional interpretation"'::jsonb, '"Treat the matter only as a Fundamental Duty"'::jsonb, '"Assess equality/non-arbitrariness under Article 14 and separately test any Article 19 restriction against its applicable constitutional grounds"'::jsonb, '"26 January 1949"'::jsonb, '"26 January 1950"'::jsonb, '"15 August 1947"'::jsonb, '"26 November 1949"'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY['0'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

-- Indian Constitution | Mid 1 | easy | TestId 440091210101012 | mcq
INSERT INTO public."TestsData" ("TestId", "Questions", "Options", "Answers")
VALUES (440091210101012, ARRAY['"A student must explain why constitutionalism matters when officials exercise emergency-like discretion. Which answer is strongest?"'::jsonb, '"Which amendment constitutionalized the Panchayati Raj framework?"'::jsonb, '"A local government officer claims their administrative decisions are outside constitutional limits because the office is local, not national. Which principle best answers that claim?"'::jsonb, '"A person challenges a deprivation of personal liberty. Which Article is most directly relevant to the stated syllabus?"'::jsonb, '"A person says all Directive Principles are individually enforceable in court because they are ''fundamental in governance''. Which reasoning corrects the conflation?"'::jsonb, '"An amendment is challenged as abolishing the essential democratic character of the Constitution. Which sequence of analysis is most appropriate for a course-level answer?"'::jsonb, '"Which of the following is a Fundamental Duty?"'::jsonb, '"A new state policy is consistent with a Directive Principle but is implemented in a way that violates Article 21. What follows?"'::jsonb, '"A claimant argues that because a policy appears in Part IV, courts must enforce it as if it were a Fundamental Right. Which constitutional text most directly challenges that claim?"'::jsonb, '"A student argues that the Preamble itself grants an unlimited legal power to an executive agency. What is the key flaw?"'::jsonb, '"What is the general legal status of Fundamental Duties?"'::jsonb, '"A parent fails to provide educational opportunities to a child aged 8. Which pair most accurately separates a Fundamental Duty from the related right?"'::jsonb, '"What is the principal purpose of a constitution?"'::jsonb, '"A constitutional amendment changes the composition of a body, and challengers claim the change damages separation of powers and judicial review. What evidence is most important to the basic-structure question?"'::jsonb, '"On which date did the Constitution of India come into effect?"'::jsonb, '"A parent or guardian is asked which Fundamental Duty concerns children''s education. Which is accurate?"'::jsonb, '"Which Article protects life and personal liberty?"'::jsonb, '"Which amendment inserted Fundamental Duties into the Constitution?"'::jsonb, '"A student says that because the Constitution is written, every rule must appear in one unamended original document. Which correction is best?"'::jsonb, '"Article 19 protects specified freedoms of:"'::jsonb, '"A state policy seeks environmental improvement, but an official arbitrarily denies access to a public benefit. What is a balanced analysis?"'::jsonb, '"An interpretation dispute involves an ambiguous provision. One interpretation better advances justice, liberty and equality while remaining consistent with the text. How may the Preamble be used?"'::jsonb, '"Which body framed and adopted the Constitution before it came into force?"'::jsonb, '"Which Article lists Fundamental Duties?"'::jsonb, '"Which statement best describes a written constitution?"'::jsonb, '"Which concept means that public power is exercised under and limited by the Constitution?"'::jsonb, '"Which Article guarantees equality before the law and equal protection of the laws?"'::jsonb, '"A person is denied personal liberty under an executive order with no lawful procedure. The authority says that administrative convenience is sufficient. Which response best reflects Article 21?"'::jsonb, '"Which Article protects specified freedoms, subject to constitutional restrictions?"'::jsonb, '"On which date was the Constitution of India adopted by the Constituent Assembly?"'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"It means only local bodies are bound by laws"'::jsonb, '"It means there is no separation of functions"'::jsonb, '"It means power is structured and limited by constitutional rules, rights and institutional checks"'::jsonb, '"It means officials may ignore law if their goal seems useful"'::jsonb, '"44th Amendment"'::jsonb, '"73rd Amendment"'::jsonb, '"86th Amendment"'::jsonb, '"42nd Amendment"'::jsonb, '"Constitutionalism applies only during general elections"'::jsonb, '"Only Parliament must follow law"'::jsonb, '"Fundamental Rights apply only to Union ministers"'::jsonb, '"Public authorities at all levels must act within applicable constitutional and legal limits"'::jsonb, '"Article 51A"'::jsonb, '"Article 324"'::jsonb, '"Article 19 only, in every circumstance"'::jsonb, '"Article 21"'::jsonb, '"Part IV is actually Part III"'::jsonb, '"Article 37 expressly distinguishes their governance importance from direct court enforceability"'::jsonb, '"Only the President can decide enforceability"'::jsonb, '"Article 51A makes every policy court-enforceable"'::jsonb, '"Ask the municipal corporation to ratify the amendment"'::jsonb, '"Check only whether the amendment title contains the word democratic"'::jsonb, '"Identify the alleged basic feature and assess it under the basic structure doctrine"'::jsonb, '"Treat every amendment as automatically invalid"'::jsonb, '"To disregard public property during protests"'::jsonb, '"To protect and improve the natural environment"'::jsonb, '"To prevent scientific inquiry"'::jsonb, '"To treat every personal preference as law"'::jsonb, '"Part IV automatically overrides Part III"'::jsonb, '"Its policy objective alone does not eliminate the need to comply with applicable Fundamental Rights"'::jsonb, '"Only Parliament''s Speaker can evaluate it"'::jsonb, '"Article 21 does not apply to government action"'::jsonb, '"Article 37"'::jsonb, '"Article 51A(k)"'::jsonb, '"Article 324"'::jsonb, '"Article 21"'::jsonb, '"The Preamble expresses constitutional values and aids interpretation; it does not independently grant unlimited executive authority"'::jsonb, '"The Preamble overrides all operative Articles"'::jsonb, '"The Preamble is the same as Article 51A"'::jsonb, '"Only the Preamble sets out local election procedures"'::jsonb, '"They are private recommendations