ns"'::jsonb, '"Convenience always overrides liberty"'::jsonb, '"Article 21 concerns only the right to vote"'::jsonb, '"Personal liberty cannot be deprived except according to procedure established by law"'::jsonb, '"42nd Amendment, Part IVA/Article 51A"'::jsonb, '"44th Amendment, Part II"'::jsonb, '"73rd Amendment, Article 19"'::jsonb, '"74th Amendment, Article 21"'::jsonb, '"Power, duty, faith and discipline"'::jsonb, '"Security, growth, wealth and unity"'::jsonb, '"Justice, liberty, equality and fraternity"'::jsonb, '"Liberty, authority, property and order"'::jsonb, '"They replace all Fundamental Rights"'::jsonb, '"They apply only to local bodies"'::jsonb, '"They are private recommendations outside the Constitution"'::jsonb, '"They are constitutional duties in Part IVA, generally not directly enforceable like Fundamental Rights"'::jsonb, '"Article 14 abolishes all classification"'::jsonb, '"Article 14 only concerns local elections"'::jsonb, '"Article 14 applies only to elected officials"'::jsonb, '"Equality requires equal protection and bars arbitrary discrimination, but reasonable classification may be constitutionally permitted"'::jsonb, '"As an authority to disregard the operative text"'::jsonb, '"As a substitute for all judicial reasoning"'::jsonb, '"As a local administration manual"'::jsonb, '"As an interpretive aid that illuminates constitutional objectives while the provision''s text remains controlling"'::jsonb, '"All Fundamental Rights can be cancelled by an ordinary officer"'::jsonb, '"Some rights, including Article 19 freedoms, are subject to constitutionally specified restrictions"'::jsonb, '"Article 21 applies only to elected legislators"'::jsonb, '"Part III contains only non-binding policy aims"'::jsonb, '"Abolition of judicial review"'::jsonb, '"Justice, liberty, equality and fraternity as constitutional objectives"'::jsonb, '"Unlimited terms for every elected body"'::jsonb, '"Absolute executive discretion"'::jsonb, '"Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel"'::jso