VALUES (4400912101010117, ARRAY['"A student confuses the Chief Election Commissioner with the State Election Commissioner. Which distinction is most accurate?"'::jsonb, '"A policy objective appears in Part IV, but a petitioner wants a court order solely to enforce it as a Directive Principle. Which constitutional statement is most relevant?"'::jsonb, '"An official detains a person and relies only on a personal preference, without lawful authority or procedure. Which provision is most directly engaged?"'::jsonb, '"A citizen damages public property during a protest. Which Fundamental Duty is most directly relevant to the conduct?"'::jsonb, '"The Prime Minister''s Council of Ministers loses a confidence vote in Lok Sabha. Which constitutional principle is most directly implicated?"'::jsonb, '"A policy objective is listed as a Directive Principle and is consistent with a Fundamental Right. Which approach best reflects the Constitution''s framework?"'::jsonb, '"A person argues that a Fundamental Right can never be limited. Which response best fits the course topics?"'::jsonb, '"An amendment changes a constitutional provision but is challenged for damaging the Constitution''s basic structure. Which doctrine is most relevant?"'::jsonb, '"A bill concerning ordinary Union governance is being studied. Which distinction between Parliament and the executive is correct?"'::jsonb, '"A parent or guardian is asked which Fundamental Duty concerns children''s education. Which is accurate?"'::jsonb, '"A general election to the Lok Sabha is being conducted, and a separate city municipal election is scheduled. Which bodies have the respective constitutional roles?"'::jsonb, '"A policy proposal concerns village-level elected self-government. Which amendment is most directly connected with the Panchayat framework?"'::jsonb, '"A legal complaint concerns both an arbitrary procedure affecting liberty and unequal treatment under law. Which Articles are most directly relevant?"'::jsonb, '"A student says Fundamental Duties and Fundamental Rights are identical because both appear in the Constitution. Which correction is strongest?"'::jsonb, '"An amendment is challenged as destroying a foundational feature such as constitutional supremacy. Which case-law doctrine is relevant to the course''s basic-structure topic?"'::jsonb, '"Which statement best describes the ECI''s constitutional role?"'::jsonb, '"A public authority refuses the same legal protection to two people in materially identical circumstances without a relevant reason. Which constitutional principle is most directly raised?"'::jsonb, '"A Governor receives advice from a state''s Council of Ministers for ordinary state executive business. Which official is the normal political head of that Council?"'::jsonb, '"The Constitution''s Preamble is invoked to interpret an ambiguous provision. Which description best fits its role?"'::jsonb, '"A person argues that the Constitution exists only to empower the government. Which Preamble value most clearly contradicts an unlimited-power view?"'::jsonb, '"A district administration office is implementing state policy and coordinating local public services. Which level is most directly represented?"'::jsonb, '"A district officer administers relief in the district and coordinates local departments. Which syllabus topic is most directly illustrated?"'::jsonb, '"A state makes policy to improve public health and welfare. Which constitutional part is especially relevant as guiding principles for State policy?"'::jsonb, '"A school textbook says Fundamental Duties were added to the Constitution through an amendment. Which pairing is correct?"'::jsonb, '"A municipality''s constitutional framework is being discussed. Which Part was added for urban local bodies by the 74th Amendment?"'::jsonb, '"A State Election Commission plans local-body elections, but a student says Article 324 alone assigns the ECI all elections of every kind. Which correction is best?"'::jsonb, '"A public authority treats people unequally and also restricts a citizen''s speech. Which two provisions are the most direct starting points for analysis?"'::jsonb, '"A local body has been asked to handle city-level services rather than district rural planning. Which institution is a better fit?"'::jsonb, '"A citizen''s speech is restricted by a law. Which is the most accurate way to evaluate the restriction under Article 19?"'::jsonb, '"A government policy promotes public health but a person argues it is a Directive Principle. Which statement best distinguishes its legal status from a Fundamental Right?"'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"The Chief Election Commissioner runs municipal elections in each city directly"'::jsonb, '"The ECI handles Parliament and State Legislature elections; State ECs handle Panchayat and municipal elections"'::jsonb, '"The State EC appoints the President"'::jsonb, '"Both are the same officer under all circumstances"'::jsonb, '"All policies in Part IV are criminal provisions"'::jsonb, '"Part IV is the same as Part III"'::jsonb, '"Article 37 states Directive Principles are not enforceable by courts, while remaining fundamental in governance"'::jsonb, '"Part IV applies only during elections"'::jsonb, '"Article 21 protection of life and personal liberty"'::jsonb, '"Article 51A only"'::jsonb, '"Article 324 only"'::jsonb, '"Article 14 only in every possible case"'::jsonb, '"Duty to serve as a judge"'::jsonb, '"Duty to vote in every election as stated in Article 51A"'::jsonb, '"Duty to protect the environment only"'::jsonb, '"Duty to safeguard public property and abjure violence"'::jsonb, '"Collective responsibility of the Union Council of Ministers to Lok Sabha"'::jsonb, '"The independence of the State Election Commission"'::jsonb, '"Fundamental Duties under Article 51A"'::jsonb, '"Governor''s appointment power"'::jsonb, '"Treat Directive Principles as automatically unenforceable in every policy decision"'::jsonb, '"Read the provisions harmoniously, recogn