VALUES (4400912101010119, ARRAY['"An amendment changes a constitutional provision but is challenged for damaging the Constitution''s basic structure. Which doctrine is most relevant?"'::jsonb, '"An official detains a person and relies only on a personal preference, without lawful authority or procedure. Which provision is most directly engaged?"'::jsonb, '"A public authority refuses the same legal protection to two people in materially identical circumstances without a relevant reason. Which constitutional principle is most directly raised?"'::jsonb, '"A parent or guardian is asked which Fundamental Duty concerns children''s education. Which is accurate?"'::jsonb, '"The Constitution''s Preamble is invoked to interpret an ambiguous provision. Which description best fits its role?"'::jsonb, '"A government policy promotes public health but a person argues it is a Directive Principle. Which statement best distinguishes its legal status from a Fundamental Right?"'::jsonb, '"Which statement best describes the ECI''s constitutional role?"'::jsonb, '"An amendment is challenged as destroying a foundational feature such as constitutional supremacy. Which case-law doctrine is relevant to the course''s basic-structure topic?"'::jsonb, '"A policy proposal concerns village-level elected self-government. Which amendment is most directly connected with the Panchayat framework?"'::jsonb, '"A district administration office is implementing state policy and coordinating local public services. Which level is most directly represented?"'::jsonb, '"A law treats a person differently based solely on an arbitrary classification unrelated to its purpose. Which constitutional concern is most directly raised?"'::jsonb, '"A local body has been asked to handle city-level services rather than district rural planning. Which institution is a better fit?"'::jsonb, '"A citizen damages public property during a protest. Which Fundamental Duty is most directly relevant to the conduct?"'::jsonb, '"A municipality''s constitutional framework is being discussed. Which Part was added for urban local bodies by the 74th Amendment?"'::jsonb, '"A student confuses the Chief Election Commissioner with the State Election Commissioner. Which distinction is most accurate?"'::jsonb, '"A student calls the President the day-to-day political head of the elected Union government. Which correction is best?"'::jsonb, '"A student says that because the Constitution is written, every rule must appear in one unamended original document. Which correction is best?"'::jsonb, '"A citizen''s speech is restricted by a law. Which is the most accurate way to evaluate the restriction under Article 19?"'::jsonb, '"A district officer administers relief in the district and coordinates local departments. Which syllabus topic is most directly illustrated?"'::jsonb, '"A policy objective is listed as a Directive Principle and is consistent with a Fundamental Right. Which approach best reflects the Constitution''s framework?"'::jsonb, '"A general election to the Lok Sabha is being conducted, and a separate city municipal election is scheduled. Which bodies have the respective constitutional roles?"'::jsonb, '"A public authority treats people unequally and also restricts a citizen''s speech. Which two provisions are the most direct starting points for analysis?"'::jsonb, '"A school textbook says Fundamental Duties were added to the Constitution through an amendment. Which pairing is correct?"'::jsonb, '"A bill concerning ordinary Union governance is being studied. Which distinction between Parliament and the executive is correct?"'::jsonb, '"A proposal is passed only by Lok Sabha, but the student claims it has therefore been passed by Parliament in every case. What must be considered?"'::jsonb, '"A city council handles local services, while rural district local affairs are handled through a Zila Panchayat. Which distinction is correct?"'::jsonb, '"A teacher is describing an amendment''s constitutional history. Which pair is correct?"'::jsonb, '"A city''s municipal poll date is announced. A student asks whether the ECI or State EC is normally constitutionally responsible. Which is correct?"'::jsonb, '"A citizen seeks to challenge restrictions on peaceful expression. What must a constitutional analysis identify before judging validity?"'::jsonb, '"A state makes policy to improve public health and welfare. Which constitutional part is especially relevant as guiding principles for State policy?"'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Doctrine of double taxation only"'::jsonb, '"Basic structure doctrine"'::jsonb, '"Doctrine of colourable printing"'::jsonb, '"Principle of absolute parliamentary supremacy"'::jsonb, '"Article 21 protection of life and personal liberty"'::jsonb, '"Article 51A only"'::jsonb, '"Article 324 only"'::jsonb, '"Article 14 only in every possible case"'::jsonb, '"Freedom of speech under Article 19 only"'::jsonb, '"Fundamental Duty under Article 51A only"'::jsonb, '"Equality before law and equal protection under Article 14"'::jsonb, '"Election administration under Article 324"'::jsonb, '"Article 14 requires every parent to be a teacher"'::jsonb, '"Article 21A is a Fundamental Duty"'::jsonb, '"Article 19 requires free university education in every case"'::jsonb, '"Article 51A(k) addresses providing educational opportunities to a child/ward aged 6–14"'::jsonb, '"A local-government regulation"'::jsonb, '"A source of unrestricted executive power"'::jsonb, '"A separate criminal code replacing all Articles"'::jsonb, '"A useful aid expressing constitutional objectives and values, read with the text rather than replacing it"'::jsonb, '"Directive Principles apply only to citizens'' private conduct"'::jsonb, '"Every Directive Principle is an offence provision"'::jsonb, '"A Directive Principle guides state policy but is not directly enforceable in the same way as a Fundamental Right"'::jsonb, '"Directive Principles always override every Fundamental Right"'::jsonb, '"It administers all municipal services"'::jsonb, '"It makes all criminal laws"'::jsonb, '"It appoints all Governors"'::jsonb, '"It supervises specified electoral rolls and elections under Article 324"'::jsonb, '"Doctrine of parliamentary privilege only"'::jsonb, '"Basic structure doctrine"'::jsonb, '"Local election rotation"'::jsonb, '"Directive Principles'' non-justiciability"'::jsonb, '"52nd Amendment"'::jsonb, '"73rd Amendment"'::jsonb, '"74th Amendment"'::jsonb, '"42nd Amendment"'::jsonb, '"Supreme Court Registry"'::jsonb, '"Municipal Corporation only in every case"'::jsonb, '"Union Legislature"'::jsonb, '"District administration"'::jsonb, '"Article 14 equality and non-arbitrariness"'::jsonb, '"Article 51A environmental duty"'::jsonb, '"The definition of a Municipal Corporation"'::jsonb, '"Article 324 election control"'::jsonb, '"Municipal Corporation"'::jsonb, '"Rajya Sabha"'::jsonb, '"Union Council of Ministers"'::jsonb, '"Zila Panchayat"'::jsonb, '"Duty to vote in every election as stated in Article 51A"'::jsonb, '"Duty to protect the environment only"'::jsonb, '"Duty to safeguard public property and abjure violence"'::jsonb, '"Duty to serve as a judge"'::jsonb, '"Part II"'::jsonb, '"Part IXA"'::jsonb, '"Part III"'::jsonb, '"Part IVA"'::jsonb, '"The ECI handles Parliament and State Legislature elections; State ECs handle Panchayat and municipal elections"'::jsonb, '"The Chief Election Commissioner runs municipal elections in each city directly"'::jsonb, '"The State EC appoints the President"'::jsonb, '"Both are the same officer under all circumstances"'::jsonb, '"The Chief Election Commissioner leads the Council of Ministers"'::jsonb, '"The Prime Minister leads the government while the President is the constitutional head"'::jsonb, '"The Speaker runs the Union ministries"'::jsonb, '"The Chief Justice is day-to-day executive head"'::jsonb, '"Amendments automatically replace all Fundamental Rights"'::jsonb, '"Only Governors can amend the Constitution"'::jsonb, '"Written 